WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:04.652 --> 00:00:07.917 line:88% position:50% align:center
Lesson two: project and team management.

2
00:00:08.952 --> 00:00:12.210 line:88% position:50% align:center
In this lesson, you'll learn
how projects are created,

3
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:15.075 line:88% position:50% align:center
how responsibility is
assigned to team leaders,

4
00:00:15.085 --> 00:00:18.493 line:88% position:50% align:center
and how existing projects
are organised and monitored.

5
00:00:20.452 --> 00:00:25.709 line:88% position:50% align:center
Before we begin, it helps to separate
three activities that are easy to confuse.

6
00:00:26.752 --> 00:00:30.349 line:88% position:50% align:center
Creating a project records
what the work is: its name,

7
00:00:30.359 --> 00:00:33.819 line:88% position:50% align:center
references, location, client and budget.

8
00:00:34.852 --> 00:00:38.501 line:88% position:50% align:center
Assigning responsibility links
that project to a team leader,

9
00:00:38.511 --> 00:00:41.190 line:88% position:50% align:center
who becomes accountable
for its field activity.

10
00:00:42.252 --> 00:00:45.614 line:88% position:50% align:center
And monitoring is the ongoing
work of following progress,

11
00:00:45.624 --> 00:00:49.306 line:88% position:50% align:center
activity and spending, until
the project is complete.

12
00:00:50.352 --> 00:00:54.951 line:88% position:50% align:center
In the platform, creating projects and
assigning team leaders are carried out by

13
00:00:54.961 --> 00:00:56.299 line:88% position:50% align:center
administrators.

14
00:00:57.819 --> 00:01:02.249 line:88% position:50% align:center
To create a project, start from the
Home dashboard or the Projects page,

15
00:01:02.259 --> 00:01:04.169 line:88% position:50% align:center
and select New Project.

16
00:01:05.585 --> 00:01:07.847 line:88% position:50% align:center
The New Project form opens.

17
00:01:08.348 --> 00:01:10.362 line:88% position:50% align:center
Let's go through each field.

18
00:01:11.385 --> 00:01:14.318 line:88% position:50% align:center
Project Name is the name
everyone will recognise,

19
00:01:14.328 --> 00:01:15.704 line:88% position:50% align:center
and it's required.

20
00:01:16.205 --> 00:01:19.587 line:88% position:50% align:center
In our example, the project is KISUMU_NITA.

21
00:01:20.619 --> 00:01:25.498 line:88% position:50% align:center
SMP is the project's SMP reference
number, and it's also required.

22
00:01:25.999 --> 00:01:29.413 line:88% position:50% align:center
The PO Number — the purchase
order — is optional,

23
00:01:29.423 --> 00:01:31.113 line:88% position:50% align:center
and can be added later.

24
00:01:32.152 --> 00:01:35.215 line:88% position:50% align:center
Site Module Package
describes the type of work

25
00:01:35.225 --> 00:01:38.346 line:88% position:50% align:center
— in this case, TI Cabinet Installation.

26
00:01:39.385 --> 00:01:42.552 line:88% position:50% align:center
Region and Location describe
where the work takes place,

27
00:01:42.562 --> 00:01:45.124 line:88% position:50% align:center
and Client records who the work is for.

28
00:01:46.185 --> 00:01:50.439 line:88% position:50% align:center
Budget is the project's allocated
budget, in Kenyan shillings.

29
00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:55.546 line:88% position:50% align:center
This figure becomes the starting point for
all of the project's financial reporting.

30
00:01:56.585 --> 00:01:58.964 line:88% position:50% align:center
Start and end dates are optional.

31
00:01:59.465 --> 00:02:03.394 line:88% position:50% align:center
If you enter both, the end date
must come after the start date.

32
00:02:04.785 --> 00:02:09.795 line:88% position:50% align:center
Further down, the Team Leader list lets
you assign responsibility straight away.

33
00:02:10.295 --> 00:02:12.902 line:88% position:50% align:center
If the right team leader
hasn't been added yet,

34
00:02:12.912 --> 00:02:16.320 line:88% position:50% align:center
leave it as Unassigned, and
assign the project later.

35
00:02:17.352 --> 00:02:21.841 line:88% position:50% align:center
Add a short description to give context
to anyone reviewing the project.

36
00:02:22.341 --> 00:02:27.181 line:88% position:50% align:center
Then choose a status: Active,
Draft, On Hold or Completed.

37
00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.319 line:88% position:50% align:center
Most new projects start as Active.

38
00:02:31.385 --> 00:02:33.725 line:88% position:50% align:center
Finally, select Create.

39
00:02:34.226 --> 00:02:38.369 line:88% position:50% align:center
The project is saved, a matching budget
record is created for its financial

40
00:02:38.379 --> 00:02:41.748 line:88% position:50% align:center
tracking, and the action is
written to the audit log.

41
00:02:42.785 --> 00:02:46.525 line:88% position:50% align:center
If a team leader was selected,
and has a phone number on record,

42
00:02:46.535 --> 00:02:50.386 line:88% position:50% align:center
they also receive an SMS letting
them know they've been assigned.

43
00:02:51.785 --> 00:02:54.861 line:88% position:50% align:center
The new project now appears
on the Projects page:

44
00:02:54.871 --> 00:02:57.536 line:88% position:50% align:center
the organisation's project portfolio.

45
00:02:58.585 --> 00:03:01.648 line:88% position:50% align:center
Filter chips let you
narrow the list by status

46
00:03:01.658 --> 00:03:05.697 line:88% position:50% align:center
— all, active, pending
approval, completed, on hold,

47
00:03:05.707 --> 00:03:10.680 line:88% position:50% align:center
or draft. Each chip shows how
many projects are in that state.

48
00:03:11.719 --> 00:03:18.030 line:88% position:50% align:center
The search box filters projects by
name, SMP, PO number or module package.

49
00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:23.085 line:88% position:50% align:center
The search bar at the very top does the
same, from anywhere in the platform.

50
00:03:24.119 --> 00:03:28.432 line:88% position:50% align:center
Each project card shows the
project name, its SMP reference,

51
00:03:28.442 --> 00:03:32.657 line:88% position:50% align:center
the module package, its status,
and the assigned team leader.

52
00:03:33.158 --> 00:03:37.894 line:88% position:50% align:center
Here, the team leader shows a dash,
meaning nobody has been assigned yet.

53
00:03:38.919 --> 00:03:42.242 line:88% position:50% align:center
Underneath are a progress
bar, the allocated budget,

54
00:03:42.252 --> 00:03:43.981 line:88% position:50% align:center
and the remaining balance.

55
00:03:45.019 --> 00:03:49.072 line:88% position:50% align:center
Understand the progress bar
clearly: it's an activity indicator,

56
00:03:49.082 --> 00:03:51.474 line:88% position:50% align:center
not a measurement of physical completion.

57
00:03:51.974 --> 00:03:55.024 line:88% position:50% align:center
It's calculated from the
number of daily logs submitted,

58
00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:58.657 line:88% position:50% align:center
it never shows more than ninety
per cent while a project is active,

59
00:03:58.667 --> 00:04:02.537 line:88% position:50% align:center
and it only reaches one hundred per cent
when an administrator approves the project

60
00:04:02.547 --> 00:04:03.650 line:88% position:50% align:center
as complete.

61
00:04:05.052 --> 00:04:07.432 line:88% position:50% align:center
Next, let's add a team leader.

62
00:04:07.932 --> 00:04:10.995 line:88% position:50% align:center
On the Team Leaders page,
or from the dashboard,

63
00:04:11.005 --> 00:04:12.902 line:88% position:50% align:center
select Add Team Leader.

64
00:04:14.285 --> 00:04:17.335 line:88% position:50% align:center
Enter the team leader's full
name, their phone number,

65
00:04:17.345 --> 00:04:19.477 line:88% position:50% align:center
and a contact email address.

66
00:04:19.977 --> 00:04:24.186 line:88% position:50% align:center
Phone numbers are automatically converted
to the international Kenyan format,

67
00:04:24.196 --> 00:04:26.588 line:88% position:50% align:center
starting with plus two five four.

68
00:04:27.619 --> 00:04:29.790 line:88% position:50% align:center
Next, choose a username.

69
00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:34.473 line:88% position:50% align:center
This becomes the team leader's sign-in
name, and the system creates their sign-in

70
00:04:34.483 --> 00:04:37.266 line:88% position:50% align:center
address by adding @newl.africa.

71
00:04:38.285 --> 00:04:40.573 line:88% position:50% align:center
You don't set a password yourself.

72
00:04:41.074 --> 00:04:45.985 line:88% position:50% align:center
The system generates one automatically,
saves it with the team leader's profile,

73
00:04:45.995 --> 00:04:50.003 line:88% position:50% align:center
and sends it to them by SMS,
together with the sign-in link.

74
00:04:51.052 --> 00:04:55.333 line:88% position:50% align:center
You can also tick the projects this
team leader will be responsible for.

75
00:04:56.385 --> 00:05:00.607 line:88% position:50% align:center
When you select Create, the system asks
you to confirm your own administrator

76
00:05:00.617 --> 00:05:04.418 line:88% position:50% align:center
password. This is a deliberate safety check.

77
00:05:05.452 --> 00:05:08.593 line:88% position:50% align:center
Because a new sign-in account
is created at this point,

78
00:05:08.603 --> 00:05:12.591 line:88% position:50% align:center
you'll then be asked to re-enter your
administrator password once more to continue

79
00:05:12.601 --> 00:05:17.378 line:88% position:50% align:center
your session. The new credentials
are also copied to your clipboard.

80
00:05:18.785 --> 00:05:21.965 line:88% position:50% align:center
Each team leader has a card
on the Team Leaders page,

81
00:05:21.975 --> 00:05:24.823 line:88% position:50% align:center
showing their contact details and username.

82
00:05:25.852 --> 00:05:30.425 line:88% position:50% align:center
The Login Credentials panel shows the
sign-in email and the password generated for

83
00:05:30.435 --> 00:05:34.842 line:88% position:50% align:center
them. We've blurred it here, and
you should treat it the same way:

84
00:05:34.852 --> 00:05:38.435 line:88% position:50% align:center
never display it on a shared
screen, never photograph it,

85
00:05:38.445 --> 00:05:41.020 line:88% position:50% align:center
and share it only with the person concerned.

86
00:05:42.052 --> 00:05:44.770 line:88% position:50% align:center
Along the bottom are the management actions.

87
00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:50.286 line:88% position:50% align:center
Assign Projects adds or removes the projects
this team leader is responsible for,

88
00:05:50.296 --> 00:05:53.743 line:88% position:50% align:center
and each newly assigned
project triggers an SMS.

89
00:05:54.785 --> 00:06:00.992 line:88% position:50% align:center
Message sends a direct message, which arrives
both as an in-app notification and as an SMS.

90
00:06:02.019 --> 00:06:05.928 line:88% position:50% align:center
Send Credentials re-sends
the sign-in details by SMS,

91
00:06:05.938 --> 00:06:08.812 line:88% position:50% align:center
which is useful if a team
leader has lost them.

92
00:06:09.852 --> 00:06:14.210 line:88% position:50% align:center
Reset Password records a new password
on the team leader's profile.

93
00:06:14.711 --> 00:06:18.711 line:88% position:50% align:center
In the current version, confirm with your
technical team that the change has also

94
00:06:18.721 --> 00:06:21.686 line:88% position:50% align:center
been applied to their sign-in
account before you share it.

95
00:06:22.719 --> 00:06:25.229 line:88% position:50% align:center
The red button removes a team leader.

96
00:06:25.729 --> 00:06:29.664 line:88% position:50% align:center
Their projects become unassigned, and
their sign-in account must be removed

97
00:06:29.674 --> 00:06:33.538 line:88% position:50% align:center
separately by the technical
administrator in the Firebase console.

98
00:06:34.585 --> 00:06:39.705 line:88% position:50% align:center
Adding, editing, assigning, messaging and
removing team leaders are all recorded in

99
00:06:39.715 --> 00:06:40.975 line:88% position:50% align:center
the audit log.

100
00:06:42.385 --> 00:06:46.392 line:88% position:50% align:center
Once a team leader is assigned,
the project shows their name.

101
00:06:46.892 --> 00:06:51.485 line:88% position:50% align:center
On the dashboard, KISUMU_NITA now
lists Tesh as its team leader.

102
00:06:52.552 --> 00:06:56.683 line:88% position:50% align:center
Assignment can be made in three
places: when creating the project,

103
00:06:56.693 --> 00:07:01.273 line:88% position:50% align:center
when creating or editing the team leader,
or with the Assign Projects button.

104
00:07:02.319 --> 00:07:05.297 line:88% position:50% align:center
Each project has one team leader at a time.

105
00:07:05.798 --> 00:07:09.395 line:88% position:50% align:center
Assigning it to someone new
replaces the previous team leader,

106
00:07:09.405 --> 00:07:12.376 line:88% position:50% align:center
and when that change is made
through the project's Edit form,

107
00:07:12.386 --> 00:07:15.768 line:88% position:50% align:center
the previous team leader is informed by SMS.

108
00:07:17.185 --> 00:07:20.398 line:88% position:50% align:center
Selecting a project opens its detail page.

109
00:07:20.898 --> 00:07:24.430 line:88% position:50% align:center
For administrators, the top
of the page shows the budget,

110
00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:27.802 line:88% position:50% align:center
spending plus approved
funds, the remaining balance,

111
00:07:27.812 --> 00:07:29.241 line:88% position:50% align:center
and the team leader.

112
00:07:30.285 --> 00:07:33.634 line:88% position:50% align:center
Tabs organise the project's
information: Overview,

113
00:07:33.644 --> 00:07:36.401 line:88% position:50% align:center
Casuals, Logs and Financials.

114
00:07:36.902 --> 00:07:41.625 line:88% position:50% align:center
The overview shows the project
details, alongside a financial summary.

115
00:07:42.685 --> 00:07:47.206 line:88% position:50% align:center
The edit button reopens the project
form, so you can update any detail,

116
00:07:47.216 --> 00:07:48.892 line:88% position:50% align:center
including the status.

117
00:07:49.919 --> 00:07:52.774 line:88% position:50% align:center
The delete button permanently
removes the project,

118
00:07:52.784 --> 00:07:57.325 line:88% position:50% align:center
together with its casual worker
records, daily logs and budget record.

119
00:07:57.825 --> 00:08:03.082 line:88% position:50% align:center
So the system asks for confirmation,
and your administrator password, first.

120
00:08:04.119 --> 00:08:08.041 line:88% position:50% align:center
Monitoring is a habit: review
active projects regularly,

121
00:08:08.051 --> 00:08:11.062 line:88% position:50% align:center
compare the logs being
submitted with what you expect,

122
00:08:11.072 --> 00:08:14.090 line:88% position:50% align:center
and follow up early when
something looks out of place.

123
00:08:15.652 --> 00:08:19.216 line:88% position:50% align:center
Finally, let's look at the
complete project lifecycle.

124
00:08:20.252 --> 00:08:23.641 line:88% position:50% align:center
A project is created as
active — or as a draft,

125
00:08:23.651 --> 00:08:26.355 line:88% position:50% align:center
or on hold, if it isn't ready to start.

126
00:08:27.419 --> 00:08:31.081 line:88% position:50% align:center
While it's active, the team
leader manages casual workers,

127
00:08:31.091 --> 00:08:35.059 line:88% position:50% align:center
submits daily logs, and may
request additional funds.

128
00:08:36.119 --> 00:08:40.061 line:88% position:50% align:center
When the work is finished, the
team leader selects Mark Complete.

129
00:08:40.561 --> 00:08:45.089 line:88% position:50% align:center
The project moves to Pending Approval,
and the administrator is notified.

130
00:08:46.119 --> 00:08:50.497 line:88% position:50% align:center
The administrator then either approves
it, which marks the project as completed,

131
00:08:50.507 --> 00:08:54.677 line:88% position:50% align:center
or sends it back with a reason, which
returns it to active so the team leader can

132
00:08:54.687 --> 00:08:56.038 line:88% position:50% align:center
address the issue.

133
00:08:57.885 --> 00:09:03.044 line:88% position:50% align:center
To summarise: administrators create projects
with accurate references and budgets,

134
00:09:03.054 --> 00:09:07.895 line:88% position:50% align:center
add team leaders with their own credentials,
and assign responsibility clearly.

135
00:09:08.919 --> 00:09:12.828 line:88% position:50% align:center
Each assignment notifies the team
leader, each change is recorded,

136
00:09:12.838 --> 00:09:17.314 line:88% position:50% align:center
and each project follows a clear path
from creation to approved completion.

137
00:09:18.352 --> 00:09:20.972 line:88% position:50% align:center
In the next lesson, we'll
move into the field,

138
00:09:20.982 --> 00:09:25.979 line:88% position:50% align:center
and see how team leaders record casual
workers and submit their daily reports.

139
00:09:28.919 --> 00:09:32.939 line:88% position:50% align:center
This training experience was
produced by KEYPOLE TECHNOLOGIES.
